{
  "readme": "The look pass material library for tools/arch (materials.py). One entry per glTF material (= one draw call, one lightmap). Colours are sRGB hex. 'texture' names a CC0 set in assets-src/textures/<id>/ (<id>_diff|nor_gl|arm_<res>.jpg, docs/handover/look-textures.md); without the files the material falls back to its flat 'color'. 'tile' is the real size of one texture repeat in metres (world-space box projection into UVMap = TEXCOORD_0). 'process' recolours the photo: 'tint' is the new mean colour, 'contrast' scales the luminance detail, 'saturation' keeps that much of the photo's own chroma; 'roughness' [mean, spread] remaps the ARM green channel. 'res' is the exported size per map (0 = map not used). 'grain': 'vertical' turns the texture 90 degrees on walls (slats). 'bevel' [width m, segments] is applied to the joined mesh (harden normals). 'lightmap' forces a lightmap size (else by area); 'bakeSamples' its Cycles samples (default 512; generate.py --bake-samples overrides all, for quick tests). 'bake': false = no lightmap (emissive, glass).",
